$FG,9$A path completion was added to help the user to find a correct path.$FG$

To trigger the shell completion, type $FG,2$ALT-TAB$FG$ combo juste after a path
to find a file/directory and complete it.

Shell completion work on the shell and in current edited file.

To complete a partial path $FG,7$(not started by /)$FG$ in a file, note where the
current edited path file and start at this position !

$FG,9$Example : (current edited file path : $FG,4$/Home/myfile.HC.Z$FG,9$)

	look my file in azTempleOS ! : $FG,12$../$FG,4$azTempleOS/Shell/ShellHook.HC.Z$FG$

$FG,12$   ../$FG$ is used to return at the $FG,4$/$FG$ path from $FG,4$/Home$FG$ 
       (where the current edited file is).




If $FG,2$ALT-TAB$FG$ is pressed and nothing append, no file is adapted to complete
the path.

If more than one file start with the same research filename,
he complete the filename with the begining of filenames who match together


You can find the current key-hook $LK,"here",A="FI:::/azTempleOS/Shell/ShellHook.HC.Z"$.
If you want disable it, you can comment the $FG,1$#include$FG$ to $LK,"MakeazTempleOS.HC.Z",A="FI:::/azTempleOS/MakeazTempleOS.HC.Z"$
for $LK,"ShellImport.HC.Z",A="FI:::/azTempleOS/Shell/ShellImport.HC.Z"$.






